Granted, but 
a) I didn't get a wish (this was around level 5 of the Gnomish Mines),
b) shields of reflection are very difficult to come by, and
c) wands of sleep are just as bad, and I've died this way more often
   than anything else.  

I still maintain that getting unexpectedly zapped by a wand of death
like that adds nothing whatsoever to the game.  It's completely 
arbitrary, there was no challenge in it, and there was no way I could
have avoided it (apart from leaving the dungeon as soon as I started
the game :-)  I'm just hacked off (pardon the pun) with getting a 
really good character together, not doing anything foolish or making
any mistakes, and then being killed out of hand.

